Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraMessageFunction", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"0eed36b6-c523-4454-a1e2-5adf8dd10058"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMessageFunction"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraMessageFunction", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6054892d-3f35-448c-978f-18d4e7e4ee54"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the message relation from the observer ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to the observer ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ": each tick of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " goes to the ticks of ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " that its light rays reach. Its members are the message functions, the \
single-valued selections of the relation that preserve the order of the \
ticks.",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"6c6da96e-604e-4a5d-b79c-2597ffbe2000"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: for observers ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ", chains given as vertex lists in causal order, the message relation sends \
a tick ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") = ",
 StyleBox["E", "TI"],
 "\:207a(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") \:2229 ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ", the ticks of ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " on the future light cone of ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ". A message function is a map ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 " from the ticks ",
 StyleBox["a'", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " with a message to ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " such that ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") \[Element] ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") for every ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " in ",
 StyleBox["a'", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 " does not reverse the order: if ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " comes before ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 " on ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ", then ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") does not come after ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ") on ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"88e32010-9ad8-4ff1-904c-1e9ffe24d4a8"],

Cell["\<\
In Minkowski space a light signal from an event of one particle reaches the \
other particle at exactly one event, and the map preserves the order of the \
clocks. On a graph a light cone can meet an observer in several ticks, or in \
none: the relation is set-valued and partial, and the message functions are \
its consistent single-valued choices. There can be many, or exactly one, as \
on the diamond lattice between two parallel null lines.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8a24158e-9389-4ef3-a0af-dfeba9dc6ff8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The head holds its two observers and computes nothing. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d72adc44-ed7e-439c-b769-8d395d13b3ab"],
 " reads it on a graph:"
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"25464f30-22be-4127-b150-a8e3856283a9"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "99903401-20bf-41c9-93fe-57e8af59066c"], Cell["Property", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"077f24ab-5e85-4003-9d2b-884c4d6017ad"],
     Cell["Value", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"ed06fff0-4c79-4742-84d2-c7191ef9bae6"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "f02bd33c-3816-4604-8538-9b1ec60544af"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<Relation\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "4f86b2df-dfb5-4553-b37d-a7ad5523d642"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "d26744c4-d59e-400f-b3b3-f73f51b8550b"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the association ",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     " \[RightArrow] ",
     StyleBox["M", "TI"],
     "(",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     ") over every tick of ",
     StyleBox["a", "TI"],
     ", images in the order of ",
     StyleBox["b", "TI"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"292da465-4f92-4b7e-bfbf-83feb672e67c"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "312f71b7-3e28-4f5f-9778-c614de461d30"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<Graph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "0d09e3ae-9ce1-48cb-92b4-0acc3e2ea9a7"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "e442b584-99ad-40b9-b700-21903cc17308"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the graph of the relation: the directed edges ",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     " \[RightArrow] ",
     StyleBox["w", "TI"],
     " with ",
     StyleBox["w", "TI"],
     " \[Element] ",
     StyleBox["M", "TI"],
     "(",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     "), on the ticks of ",
     StyleBox["a", "TI"],
     " and ",
     StyleBox["b", "TI"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"23aeaf4d-9978-45e3-bddd-3f229e99ada8"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "0c9e3303-f3c1-4f56-94c8-35cf45e6a263"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<SelectionGraph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "94f9ed74-5cbd-4849-a925-805a633018aa"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "db97459b-20f3-4407-aedd-f8ee6ba866cd"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the selection graph: the directed acyclic graph whose paths from its \
source {0} to its sink are exactly the members, one layer of nodes {",
     StyleBox["i", "TI"],
     ", ",
     StyleBox["w", "TI"],
     "} per tick ",
     StyleBox["i", "TI"],
     " of ",
     StyleBox["a", "TI"],
     " with a message and one edge between consecutive layers for each pair \
of images that does not reverse the order of ",
     StyleBox["b", "TI"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"ce39265f-7dac-4c0c-8693-42f51e093681"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "4eecb05e-e692-4d26-b5c5-b3114b3dc9bb"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<Cardinality\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "825c4b22-6289-4854-992b-0e8e5e0110a2"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "f27d99be-abb3-4d90-9a00-ca4cf082573e"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the number of message functions: the number of source-to-sink paths of \
the selection graph, counted by dynamic programming over the ticks of ",
     StyleBox["a", "TI"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"b306febf-bef2-4685-973c-4ca3aa7ab04d"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "bbb5d9af-cea6-40a7-b0e8-74a1bf65c452"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<Faithful\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "9d1bebe5-3903-4601-bde2-be63321a6151"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "02041c0b-f9d5-4a9b-89f1-82a644c609c2"], Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "02b31203-e261-4e1e-8796-ca113ab1e445"],
     ": the correspondence between members and source-to-sink paths of the \
selection graph is exact"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"93c9e35e-a2a5-480c-8fc4-0245989dc91e"]}
  }]], "2ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"2753b33e-80c7-4961-ad0c-\
9b14d2030be1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A member is an association from the ticks of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " with a message to ticks of ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMessageFunctionQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraMessageFunctionQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9787ab2a-48b6-4f1f-8871-4391291dc4d0"],
 " recognises one, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["RandomInfraMessageFunction"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/RandomInfraMessageFunction", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "fa898273-7afa-4b57-aed4-384c79330b66"],
 " draws members uniformly or enumerates them, as paths of the ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<SelectionGraph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c61d6ba8-50dd-4c8c-83f1-0b63ca241f8a"],
 ": the two graphs differ in that ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Graph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e98b6173-f047-49a9-a66e-2df643bb2e32"],
 " is the relation itself, while ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<SelectionGraph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15bbee61-b11c-46ff-93ca-58de3be3221b"],
 " is the chain-head DAG through which ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Cardinality\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39d1adc4-9906-40f2-9f76-d26c9bd9568e"],
 " and the sampler read the members. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSubstrateHighlight"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSubstrateHighlight", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "df599b8c-6fce-492e-aeff-0e7cdd39ea61"],
 " draws the head as the light rays that carry its messages."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b18b8305-d8d1-406b-a2f8-f4fd4063826e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The EPS defects measure how far the relation is from a monotone bijection \
of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " onto ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ", the message function of two inertial observers in Minkowski space. They \
are read on a window of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ", the ticks that remain after the option ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<Margin\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "b"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64021a0c-735a-4116-b71a-07fb71b15b65"],
 " drops ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " ticks at each end (default 0), given as a fourth argument; the images stay \
in the whole of ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ". With ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") the image of a window tick and ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " the window size:"
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"593f5715-97ed-4727-972d-2b49e02dff93"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "3ddee6fe-d0a0-49fc-b71f-7a5df92acac7"], Cell["Property", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"1e73aa09-1c74-4a96-ba2a-848a10aedcc2"],
     Cell["Value", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"162bed24-002a-4578-bac2-a20da05f8fe7"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "368af7b2-2eca-47fd-8fe5-cd9feb1a5919"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<DomainDefect\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "2820ab89-1d42-403d-9761-66b93223299b"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "da9d99ff-49fe-484c-a7e8-262bb10a4c2c"], Cell[TextData[{
     "#{",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     " : ",
     StyleBox["M", "TI"],
     "(",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     ") = \[EmptySet]} / ",
     StyleBox["n", "TI"],
     ", the fraction of ticks without a message"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"c41f8d7b-58bc-495d-8f39-973180890ec2"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "f3391aad-4658-427d-a8ee-1f8b4cfe8e39"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<FunctionDefect\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "a053b7cc-cc96-4f49-b8a4-e676bf7a8991"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "beb83ed8-99d0-4365-b510-2f8de35c511b"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the mean over the window of max(0, |",
     StyleBox["M", "TI"],
     "(",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     ")| \[Minus] 1) / max(1, |",
     StyleBox["M", "TI"],
     "(",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     ")|), zero exactly when every image has at most one tick"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"5f43aa5f-75f9-4ee7-828f-96ab6b633476"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "bd4c3834-cdfd-4c18-8e6f-ce1497be8677"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<InjectivityDefect\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "0057d1cc-435b-4690-8f2e-1fdb39a2ed5b"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "f68f9c16-83e3-40c7-b026-5fa9c7aecbf2"], Cell[TextData[{
     "1 \[Minus] \[Nu] / ",
     StyleBox["n", "TI"],
     ", with \[Nu] the size of a maximum matching of the bipartite graph of \
the relation"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"0b8ede61-71b2-4c5d-8376-54c14ebf1d60"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "fc92f7c5-7f07-4eba-8315-51c4ce57f9d8"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<OrderDefect\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "bfaea18c-435b-473c-b859-5f7a09c95d21"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "5de3a80e-ab32-4317-97a5-d1021259d943"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the fraction of ordered tick pairs ",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     " before ",
     StyleBox["w", "TI"],
     " in the window for which some image of ",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     " comes after some image of ",
     StyleBox["w", "TI"],
     " on ",
     StyleBox["b", "TI"],
     "; equal single images are no violation"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"a44d30ab-eb5f-436a-a224-7617d2e43c55"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "f0f9686a-2637-4147-82a9-2b7b0e050a14"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<KFactor\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "34079e8d-f670-4339-9c6e-a1dc8af3996e"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "f4be4f88-54c0-4713-a771-09f25c446be6"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the ratio of received to sent tick spans of the earliest-image \
selection: with ",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     ", ",
     StyleBox["w", "TI"],
     " the first and last window ticks that have a message, (pos ",
     StyleBox["f", "TI"],
     "(",
     StyleBox["w", "TI"],
     ") \[Minus] pos ",
     StyleBox["f", "TI"],
     "(",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     ")) / (pos ",
     StyleBox["w", "TI"],
     " \[Minus] pos ",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     "), positions counted on ",
     StyleBox["b", "TI"],
     " and on ",
     StyleBox["a", "TI"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"4a9639e4-2f91-4b37-9ed0-ee7735d6adb8"]}
  }]], "2ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"e14556ad-252b-48f9-8f89-\
9416c6972bf6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The four defects lie in [0, 1]; the injectivity defect is at least the \
domain defect, since a matching uses no tick without a message. The order \
defect compares image spans weakly, so a tie, two ticks with the same single \
image, is a defect of injectivity and not of order; strict monotonicity is \
the vanishing of both. All four vanish exactly when the relation is a \
single-valued map with strictly increasing images, axiom D1 on the window, \
which is what ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["EPSMessageAxiomQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/EPSMessageAxiomQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "09ddc812-0135-4d11-a7e5-049a20e9056d"],
 " tests. The k-factor is the graph form of the Bondi factor: in Minkowski \
space an inertial observer receding at speed ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " receives the ticks of another at ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " = \[Sqrt]((1 + ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ")/(1 \[Minus] ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ")) proper seconds per second sent. On a graph the tick spans are chain \
lengths, so the reading is a clock-rate statement, and it is the Bondi factor \
only where ticks count proper time. On the diamond lattice the chain {(",
 StyleBox["m", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["m", "TI"],
 ")} at rest sends its ticks one to one to the chain {(2",
 StyleBox["m", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["m", "TI"],
 ")} of velocity 1/3, k-factor 1 instead of \[Sqrt]2, because that chain's \
ticks are \[Sqrt]2 times longer in proper time; the echo read on the resting \
clock alone recovers \[Sqrt]2, see ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraEchoFunction"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraEchoFunction", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ae96faa7-ee58-4571-8a8b-2e283cc68306"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6bb99caa-886d-4f26-85c4-3e45c815ffdc"],

Cell["Corresponding notions:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c71fe78e-249e-4517-8751-6c937e236609"],

